  "verdicts": [
    {
      "sha256": "20dd4b9da9f2bd72cb741316f5a29d660e51cb63e4f004244df0b500218c2bdf",
      "identity": "net-codec-testmetest@1.0.0",
      "verdict": "BENIGN",
      "evidence": [
        "Original tarball is 295 bytes; two ordinary regular members only. index.js only assigns module.exports={version:\"1.0.0\"}.",
        "Manifest has only a test echo command; no install hook, imports, dependencies, URLs, encoded payload or extra archive members.",
        "Original registry sidecar records near-zero adoption, three releases within 24 hours and removal. Version endpoint now returns 404. No evidence of malicious execution in these bytes.",
        "Possible source rationale: removed burst publication associated by suffix with other suspicious releases. The list alone does not establish a payload in this version."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "Keep all publication/naming/stub facts; move the removed-burst observation out of impersonation and remove unsupported attack/lifecycle mappings."
      ]
    },
    {
      "sha256": "fc5aca6066b8ae97e028ee68d64f46caee44d2a60255fc01489d6a46ac1c82a6",
      "identity": "Spider-configured native Linux DDoS bot 2.0.6",
      "verdict": "MALICIOUS",
      "evidence": [
        "Stripped static i386 ELF with uClibc. main at 0x0804d518 calls anti-debug checks at 0x0804818c and exits on tracing/timing flags, then double-forks and redirects stdio.",
        "0x080583f4 lazily recovers 269 length-prefixed fixed-stride strings: ciphertext at VA 0x08094c20, slot stride 163, lengths at VA 0x08094b00, repeating 24-byte key at VA 0x0809f767.",
        "C2 hostname and port are separately ChaCha20-encrypted. Functions 0x0804a9a4 and 0x0804a94c recover hand.genddos.st:48101.",
        "0x08049cb0 connects, sends HELLO with architecture, host fingerprint, CPU, RAM and bandwidth/storage measurements, receives line commands and passes them to 0x080490bf.",
        "!EXEC task runs sh -c with stdout/stderr piped back in EXECR replies; !ATK dispatches named UDP/TCP/HTTP/game-server flood routines through the handler registry at 0x080947a0.",
        "0x08054c3a copies the executable, writes launch scripts and activation artifacts for systemd, cron, rc.local, init and shell profiles. Formats and calls bind the staged path to launch arguments.",
        "0x0804c9d1/0x0804bbb7 inspect other processes and kill/remove rival bots and miners. 0x08055ce8 targets antivirus/rootkit scanners, sends SIGSTOP/SIGKILL and removes/disables services and launch entries.",
        "Kernel-thread names are decoded and passed to prctl(PR_SET_NAME). A watchdog child monitors the parent and reinstalls/restarts it. No runtime success was assumed."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "Recover task/response command set and decoded cron/systemd/antivirus/flood configurations using operands from executable decoder code. Key bytes, C2, process name, slot numbers, file size and table addresses are not fixed.",
        "Five hostile findings cover tasking, DDoS, antivirus interference and two distinct persistence surfaces; preserve anti-debugging and all accurate neutral observations.",
        "Add chmod INT 0x80 coverage and extend execve syscall wrapper matching; migrate path, daemon-name and game-probe facts to neutral homes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "sha256": "824dab563091954637c9d95a253ef28e41ac95e32de72b41a77fca1d26c78de8",
      "identity": "Sleipnir performance tuner 3.23.0.0 (PS2EXE)",
      "verdict": "BENIGN",
      "evidence": [
        "dnfile/dncil trace of Main token 0x06000072: read the sole managed resource Sleipnir.ps1, feed its UTF-8 text into a PowerShell runspace via AddScript/BeginInvoke; extraction switch writes the same resource. No second payload or obfuscated wrapper stage.",
        "Managed script resource is 364937 bytes of unobfuscated WPF UI, system measurements and tuning logic. User actions call Invoke-TweakApply or Invoke-ProfileRun, back up prior values locally and retain apply/revert history.",
        "Gaming/Maximum profiles add Defender game-directory/process exclusions, lower scan overhead, change services, disable selected startup entries and security mitigations. These sensitive capabilities are real and retained, including the suspicious Defender process-exclusion trait.",
        "Initial window rendering starts read-only security/dashboard/network scans; mutations are UI-triggered. Credential UI and keyboard APIs belong to the wrapper/hotkey UI, not credential theft or recording. Browser profile paths are cache-cleanup targets.",
        "Driver-install path fetches configured vendor URLs, requires a Valid Authenticode result and matching publisher, creates a restore point, then runs the installer; the configured NVIDIA and Intel URLs currently resolve to vendor HTML pages. AMD URL redirects to an official download-incomplete page and fetch fails; this path only opens a vendor page in the app.",
        "Self-elevation fetch/eval branch is guarded and configured with a non-resolving placeholder URL; the compiled requireAdministrator manifest normally makes this branch unnecessary. Other HTTP strings are XAML namespaces. No covert C2 or exfiltration was found.",
        "osslsigncode: matching Authenticode content digest and timestamp signature; code signer CN=Sleipnir Local Publisher is self-signed and fails public-root trust. Intact signature is not a trusted-publisher assertion.",
        "Corpus collection/24 detections plausibly reflect PS2EXE, elevation, security changes and self-signing. Original download/deployment context is missing; BENIGN is a content judgement suitable for sighted quarantine, not clean provenance."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "No sample-specific suppressor or security-capability downgrade. Accurate sensitive findings remain."
      ]
    }
  ],
